WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.140
- You know, this is our
a little pasta baby.

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.970
We're breathing life into this thing.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.580
Keep watching, you'll see what happens.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:06.740
Suspenseful.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.670
What's up everyone?

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:08.920
I'm chef Joe Sasto,

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.350
and today I am playing a
game called make it pasta

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.330
where we have this mystery wheel here.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.810
I'm going to spin it and then turn

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.130
whatever that is into pasta.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.480
Let's give it a whirl, huh?

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.890
Apple pie.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:26.130
Apple pie's iconic.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.090
I'm okay with that one.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.830
I'm into it. I feel it.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.680
Let's get some apple pie and
give it a little taste test.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.330
So we have our pie here.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.163
Classic.

00:00:36.163 --> 00:00:37.390
We all know what's in an apple pie.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.090
We got our apples, cinnamon,
sugar, butter, pie crust.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.070
I mean, I could cut myself a slice or

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.680
I could just go right into the center.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.933
It's my pie, I make my own decisions.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.890
Hm. Nice sweetness on the
apples, not too sugary.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.670
Soft, still got a little bit of crunch.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.380
I could do something with that.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.620
Gears are turning, I know
what we're going to do.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:03.733
Let's make it pasta.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.800
First things first here, we
got to make a pasta dough.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:09.633
I have an idea for this.

00:01:09.633 --> 00:01:11.210
I've made plenty of pasta doughs,

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:15.170
but I haven't done one quite
like this using pie crust,

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:16.070
but I have an idea.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.160
I think it's going to work.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.890
I'm gonna start by kind of dissecting

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:22.000
part of my pie here,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.000
pulling just this lattice
crust from the top.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.170
And I'm gonna put that
into a food processor.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.650
I don't want any apples.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.920
So pie crust pasta dough, super authentic.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.100
You could probably find
this nowhere in Italy.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.760
So we got flour, double O, our pie crust.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.630
We'll go here, I'm going
to use all this flour

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:43.920
cause we're kind of staying
in that apple pie world,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.840
they got a little bit of cinnamon.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.020
So our dough is going to
have like a hint of cinnamon,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.730
just a little kiss.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:51.510
I have some dry milk powder here.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.870
Kind of like carrying
those flavors, I feel like,

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:56.430
with a dessert pasta, some
milk powder would be nice.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.920
Get that flavor of milk in there.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.330
Put a little bit of salt.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.550
You always want some salt in pasta dough.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.250
Then we're going to throw the lid on and

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.253
get all that pie crust broken
up before we add our eggs.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:10.490
All right, I feel good about that.

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:12.990
It actually, it already
smells really nice.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.910
Crust is like blooming in there.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:18.310
We got our flour base and then
just like all pasta doughs,

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:19.760
we're gonna work in a little bit of egg.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.700
So I'm going to go mostly yolks and

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.780
then some whole eggs to bring it together.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.903
Starting with just the yolks.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:28.460
One at a time.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.360
And I wish I could say
I had a recipe for this,

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.133
but honestly, I'm just,
we're making it up as we go.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:35.880
This is a stage. There are no swaps.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.530
This is happening. This is a real life.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.103
So now we go whole egg.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.710
Let's go another whole egg.

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:44.530
You can see the dough's coming together.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.100
Let's stop and check the hydration here.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.700
Oh, look at that.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.810
I think we might be on
our way to pasta dough.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.890
All right, let's get all
this stuff out of the way

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.140
and we'll start kneading.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.720
Everyone's favorite part of pasta making,

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.230
we gotta knead this, we
gotta develop some gluten.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.540
So I'm going to go right
here onto our countertop.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.670
So let's bring this all together and

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.280
then just like all pasta doughs,

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.290
we're just going to
work this, kneading it.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.780
It doesn't feel too far
off from a pasta dough.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:17.030
You know, the color is a
little like untraditional

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.640
in that sense, normally you
got that like bright yellow,

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.590
and as we keep kneading,

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.400
this should smooth out and
become nice and supple.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.900
Supple and smooth.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:27.900
This is where I'd normally want to

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.880
throw it in a stand mixer.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.000
Let the machine do all the work,

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.660
but I'm doing this for you guys,

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:34.870
we're going to do this all by hand.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.520
Fatto a mano.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.120
It's our little pasta baby.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.930
We're breathing life into this thing.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:41.750
Keep watching, you'll see what happens.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:44.090
So we're getting a little
smoother all the way around there.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:47.090
We got our apple pie pasta
dough, I'm going to wrap this up.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.140
We're going to set this aside to rest

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.383
and now it's time to get
started on the filling.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.720
Let's do it.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.640
Now this I'm very excited for

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.340
cause I feel like it can be
used for more than just a

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.530
pasta filling.

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:04.370
We got our luscious,
yummy apple pie filling.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.300
We'll go all the apples
down into the food processor

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.630
to kind of like bulk this up,

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.090
make sure I have enough for all my pasta,

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:13.400
add a nice kind of creamy richness to it,

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.030
I'm going go one of my
favorite pasta filling bases,

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.660
we'll go a little bit of ricotta,

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.940
some mascarpone cheese.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.730
So essentially we're making a
apple ricotta cannoli filling.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:25.770
A little bit of salt.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.570
I'm going to use some vanilla bean paste.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:30.420
You could use vanilla bean extract,

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.040
you could use vanilla beans.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.750
Now we got powdered sugar,

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.600
just to sweeten things up in there.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.920
I know there's already
sugar on the apples,

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.750
but we got those two new cheeses in here

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:40.950
that can be a little bland.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:45.040
I don't want it to be savory,
we're going sweet pasta dolce.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.480
Dessert pasta.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.810
And yes, for all of
you Italians out there,

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.640
sweet pasta is a thing.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:51.763
Trust me on that one.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.570
Look at that.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:55.930
I mean that's pasta filling.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:57.680
Let's give it a quick little taste.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.970
I'm just going to go drink this.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:03.470
No, actually we're going to
put it into a piping bag and

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.492
then I want, we'll make one
more component for our pasta.

00:05:06.492 --> 00:05:07.800
I'm gonna use the rest of that crust

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.793
to make a crumble rumble topping.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.620
Let's make some streusel.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.010
So, if you know me,

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:16.670
you know I'm a big fan
of some crumble rumble.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:17.850
I like texture.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.320
Now in the world of apple pie,

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.180
I feel like there are those
two schools of thought.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:23.160
You have that streusely topping,

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.960
which some people might
call a cobbler or crumble,

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.660
an apple crumble or crisp.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.210
Sometimes you find that lattice crust,

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.420
where it's all pie dough.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:34.470
So I'm going to try to fuse
and mold the two together

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.410
by using my pie crust that's leftover

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.830
to make a streusel like topping

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:42.300
to go on top of our dessert pasta.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.320
Sound good, yeah?

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.460
I feel really good about this.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:45.770
I don't know. How do you feel?

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:48.750
So we got the rest of our
crust down into a bowl

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.030
we just go a little bit
of all-purpose flour,

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.940
maybe a lot a bit of all purpose flour.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:54.940
Making it up. There are
no recipes for this.

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:56.240
We got some brown sugar.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.850
You got some white sugar.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:00.680
Little pinch of salt.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.430
I have melted butter.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:03.730
This is going to make things even better

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:06.460
cause butter is better and more delicious.

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:07.293
Oh yeah.

00:06:07.293 --> 00:06:08.830
If you want to double down on the butter,

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:09.970
I'm not gonna judge you.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:11.100
I support that decision.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.890
One of my favorite spices,
a little bit of nutmeg.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.720
Warm some things up here.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.500
We just want to give this a nice mix.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:21.400
Crumble up all that pie crust.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.160
I almost want to eat this by the handful,

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.350
but self-control all right?

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.520
I'm gonna throw this onto a baking sheet.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.820
I don't mind some big chunks in there.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.260
You could always break it up a little bit.

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:34.100
Spread that out so it bakes evenly.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.820
I'm going to pop this into the
oven while this is baking and

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:38.260
the dough is resting.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.960
I have one more thing to
make this a little extra.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.020
We're gonna make a caramel sauce

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.623
to drizzle on top of our pasta.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.030
We just got some white sugar.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:50.780
We're going down into the
bottom of a pot or pan.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:52.070
And we're going to let that sugar melt,

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:53.230
the water is going to cook off,

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:55.060
the sugar is going to start to caramelize.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.880
We're going to hit it with a
little cream, a little butter,

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.040
make it nice and luscious.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:01.693
Then we'll have the perfect
topping for our pasta.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.190
Sugar is caramelized.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.180
We got that dark amber.

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.860
Things are gonna get wild real quick

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.603
as soon as we add this cream.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:16.860
So cream is in there,
our pan is cooled down.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:18.240
Caramel is on its way.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.100
We'll add a little bit of butter.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:22.990
I'm going to season this
up with a little salt,

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:24.960
a little bit of salt in sweet things

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.650
make them taste sweeter.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.840
A little bit of sugar in savory things,

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.730
make them taste more savory.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:33.800
And then we're just using
that carry over heat,

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.173
melt in our butter.

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:41.280
Look at that. Salted caramel.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:44.040
Who doesn't love apples and caramel?

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:47.090
So this we're just going
to put here in our bowl and

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:49.040
save until we're ready.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:50.640
It's like a caramel hot tub in there.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:53.333
Time to make some pasta,
bring this all together.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.200
Our dough has been resting.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.153
We can remove it here from our wrap.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:01.890
Look at that.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:03.920
Pasta dough and we're done. That's it.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:04.753
You can all go home.

00:08:04.753 --> 00:08:07.670
No, just kidding, we'll turn
it into pasta shapes now.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.960
We'll get a little bit of flour down.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.180
This is my favorite part.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:14.450
I always like to start it
off just with a rolling pin

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:16.900
to get us going.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:19.163
I'm going to go split it in half.

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.520
So I'm gonna keep this in here

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.366
just so it doesn't dry out.

00:08:24.366 --> 00:08:27.283
(machine whirring)

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:31.640
There we go.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:36.960
Our apple pie cinnamon crust pasta dough.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.270
A combination of words

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:40.100
I didn't think I would ever say out loud

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:41.660
and yet here we are.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:45.420
Now, all we gotta do is get
this cut up into pieces and

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.543
make some caramelle.

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:49.263
And you know what?

00:08:49.263 --> 00:08:51.610
Before anyone asks, all his
trim, we're going to eat it.

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:52.800
We're making chef snacks.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:56.323
We're not wasting anything.
Everybody calm down.

00:08:57.210 --> 00:08:58.883
I'm a professional, all right?

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:03.923
So we have our apple pie filling.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:07.820
Give this a little spray

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:10.040
and that's going to help
us to seal our dough.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.960
For everybody following along,

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:14.460
your folding over the rectangle,

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:18.800
I want to seal down
that first notch or flap

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:21.511
combining the two layers into
one, folding that over itself,

00:09:21.511 --> 00:09:25.210
and then we're going to
seal the sides again.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.800
Now combining the four
layers down into two.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.960
So our thickness is, cook well,

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.340
and then we're just pinching
up and squeezing the sides

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.710
to flare out the ends
like a candy wrapper.

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:36.870
Like everything, you know,

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:38.970
the more you practice, the better you get.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:41.960
The moment I've been waiting for,

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:43.080
hopefully we've all been waiting for,

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.770
we're going to cook these, plate these

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.250
and give them an official taste test.

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.530
Just like the start of
every really great thing,

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.140
we're going to make
some brown butter here.

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:53.850
Let's get a nice little
couple of tablespoons

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.330
down in the bottom of the pan.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:56.320
And you know what?

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.330
If you're at home and you
want to make this ala mode,

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.600
I support that decision.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.970
So we've got our butter heating up,

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:03.770
the water's going to evaporate,

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:05.380
those milk solids are going to separate,

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:07.400
they're going to float
to the bottom of the pan,

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.860
all that's going to start
to toast and caramelize

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:13.560
and right before our eyes
we'll have brown butter.

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:17.540
We're getting all this beautiful,
wonderful, nutty flavor.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:19.550
We'll keep it on the lighter
side of brown butter.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.513
Set this aside, boil some
water and cook some pasta.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.310
Boiling water, little
bit of salt in this case,

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:29.520
I don't need it like totally seasoned

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.200
as if I was cooking a savory pasta,

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:33.200
but a little bit of salt goes a long way.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:36.710
We will drop our noods down there.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:37.720
Go noods, go.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.560
Now fresh pasta only is going
to take a couple of minutes.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.570
As soon as we see these float,

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:44.933
we should be able to go
right into our brown butter,

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.610
caramelle in the butter and

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:50.170
a little bit of that starchy pasta water

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.250
emulsify together with the brown butter.

